Package: cpxy-gateway
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: cpxy-ng <https://github.com/simophin/cpxy-ng>
Depends: iproute2
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/simophin/cpxy-ng
Description: cpxy for traffic a Linux box forwards, such as a Tailscale exit node's
 Routes forwarded TCP from chosen interfaces (tailscale0 by default) through a cpxy server, with
 local-region traffic going direct, and makes cpxy-dns-split the box's resolver so exit-node
 clients get split DNS. Configure /etc/cpxy/cpxy.conf, then enable cpxy-router and
 cpxy-dns-split. Stopping or removing them restores the original setup.
